mintcare (1.11.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Assistant: can run MintCare's read-only checks when allowed (output
    scrubbed of names, serials and MAC addresses), adaptive thinking with a
    "Think harder" option, and the cost of each answer.
  * Desktop tweaks for your account: turn off Cinnamon effects; full-screen
    games skip the compositor (added to the Gaming profile).
  * Cleaner: data left by removed Flatpak apps, unused Cinnamon add-ons
    (both opt-in, moved to the Trash).
  * Disk space: Old downloads tab; restore single files from Timeshift.
  * Startup apps can start 10 s, 30 s or 1 min after login.
  * Backup: restore files, folders or a whole snapshot without losing what
    they replace.
  * Security: names from outside MintCare (processes, files, Flatpak apps)
    can no longer run commands in root steps; private reports and the
    assistant no longer show passwords in software source addresses.

 -- Matthew Allwood <matthewallwood@protonmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:05:33 +0100

mintcare (1.10.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * SMART trend: drive error counters are recorded and a warning appears
    when reallocated, pending, uncorrectable, media or CRC errors grow.
  * Security: Identify now explains unknown listening ports (program,
    owning package, systemd service) and suggests keeping or turning off.
  * Troubleshoot: internet speed test (download, upload, latency).
  * Mint upgrade checklist: held and half-installed packages, DKMS drivers,
    battery power.
  * Releases carry SHA256SUMS and a signed build-provenance attestation;
    packaging/ppa.sh builds Launchpad source packages.
  * README screenshots. Tests never touch the real ~/.config or ~/.local.

